(Status: short guide.) '
() '
(Cyberdeck OS keeps one Debian system on the disk. When a program is packaged for Ubuntu, Arch, or an) '
() '
(The image includes Distrobox and Podman.) '
() '
(Create an Ubuntu container and open a shell in it:) '
() '
(sh) '
(distrobox create --name ubuntu --image ubuntu:24.04) '
(distrobox enter ubuntu) '
() '
() '
(Arch is the same idea:) '
() '
(sh) '
(distrobox create --name arch --image archlinux:latest) '
(distrobox enter arch) '
() '
() '
(Programs installed inside the container stay there. The host apt sources stay Debian 13, plus the ve) '
() '
(Requirements: [the specification]\(../SPEC.md\), section 9.) '
() '
